! Scroll Memory -- never lose your place

Long tiddlers cost you your place: you follow a link, come back, and have to hunt for the sentence you left. Scroll Memory remembers how deep you were reading, and records a landmark whenever you follow a link out of a long tiddler. A floating button returns you to the exact view you had, with the clicked link blinking to mark the spot. Closing a tiddler that a link opened brings you back automatically, and while you are editing a toggle steps between your open drafts and the last landmark, so you can read a source and write about it side by side.
